From: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
Subject: aic8800_btlpm: add soft dependency on aic8800_bsp

aic8800_bsp powers the AIC8800 and loads the Bluetooth firmware patch via
SDIO. It is pulled in as a dependency of the WiFi driver aic8800_fdrv, but
aic8800_btlpm does not use any of its symbols. Hence, when WiFi is not used,
loading aic8800_btlpm alone leaves the Bluetooth core without firmware patch,
and it does not respond to HCI commands. Declare the soft dependency, so that
modprobe loads aic8800_bsp first.

Signed-off-by: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_btlpm/aic8800_btlpm.c b/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_btlpm/aic8800_btlpm.c
index 7ec7c91..ad02040 100644
--- a/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_btlpm/aic8800_btlpm.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_btlpm/aic8800_btlpm.c
@@ -1226,6 +1226,8 @@ module_init(bluesleep_init);
 module_exit(bluesleep_exit);
 
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Bluetooth Sleep Mode Driver ver %s " VERSION);
+/* The Bluetooth firmware patch is loaded by aic8800_bsp, also when WiFi (aic8800_fdrv) is not used */
+MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: aic8800_bsp");
 #ifdef MODULE_LICENSE
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
 #endif
